Q: How can I implement automatically numbered headings in Confluence A: <p>You can extend the original solution by adding a small function that removes any numbering at the beginning of a heading before the script applies the new index. This allows the numbering to be regenerated cleanly every time the script runs.</p>
<p>Full script:</p>
<pre><code>(function () {
  function stripExistingNumbering(str) {
    return str
      .replace(/^[\s\u00A0]+/, &quot;&quot;)
      .replace(/^\d+(?:\.\d+)*\.\s+/, &quot;&quot;);
  }

  function addIndex() {
    const indices = [];

    jQuery(&quot;.ak-editor-content-area .ProseMirror&quot;)
      .find(&quot;h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6&quot;)
      .each(function () {
        const level = parseInt(this.nodeName.substring(1), 10) - 1;

        if (indices.length - 1 &gt; level) {
          indices.length = level + 1;
        }

        if (indices[level] === undefined) {
          indices[level] = 0;
        }

        indices[level]++;

        const cleanText = stripExistingNumbering(jQuery(this).text().trim());
        jQuery(this).text(indices.join(&quot;.&quot;) + &quot;. &quot; + cleanText);
      });
  }

  addIndex();
})();
</code></pre>
<p>Bookmarklet version (one-liner):</p>
<pre><code>javascript:(function(){function stripExistingNumbering(str){return str.replace(/^[\s\u00A0]+/,&quot;&quot;).replace(/^\d+(?:\.\d+)*\.\s+/,&quot;&quot;)}function addIndex(){const indices=[];jQuery(&quot;.ak-editor-content-area .ProseMirror&quot;).find(&quot;h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6&quot;).each(function(){const level=parseInt(this.nodeName.substring(1),10)-1;if(indices.length-1&gt;level){indices.length=level+1}if(indices[level]===undefined){indices[level]=0}indices[level]++;const cleanText=stripExistingNumbering(jQuery(this).text().trim());jQuery(this).text(indices.join(&quot;.&quot;)+&quot;. &quot;+cleanText)})}addIndex()})();
</code></pre>
<p>This enhancement removes patterns like <code>1.</code>, <code>1.2.</code> or <code>1.2.3.</code> from the start of headings before numbering is applied, allowing the script to be executed repeatedly while always regenerating consistent numbering.</p>

